POSTS[0:0]=[
("php2shell-explained","PHP2Shell explained: why websites went dark to patch this week","Two critical PHP flaws let attackers take over web servers. What PHP2Shell is, why it's trending, which versions fix it and where to follow it.","tech-ai","php2shell-vulnerability","PHP2Shell: sites go dark to patch","PHP",PHP_SRC,
"""<p>If a few of your favorite sites blinked out this week, here's probably why. Two serious bugs turned up in <b>PHP</b>, the language quietly running a huge share of the web, and site owners everywhere scrambled to patch.</p>
<h2>What it is</h2>
<p>The flaws are tracked as <b>CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619</b>, and researchers nicknamed them PHP2Shell. In plain English, they could let a stranger run their own code on a web server without a password. On October 21, the U.S. cybersecurity agency CISA told everyone to update to <b>PHP 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 or 8.2.35</b> right away, and said PHP 8.1 and older have no fix at all.</p>
<table><tr><th>Fixed versions</th><td>8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36, 8.2.35</td></tr><tr><th>PHP 8.1 or older</th><td>No patch; take it offline</td></tr><tr><th>Found by</th><td>Calif and Wiz researchers, using AI</td></tr><tr><th>Exploited?</th><td>Not seen by CISA at publication; Cloudflare's CTO told the BBC early attacks were emerging</td></tr></table>
<h2>Why it's trending</h2>
<p>Three things made this huge. The bugs sat unnoticed for more than a decade. Details leaked on social media before the fix was ready, which forced an early announcement. And the researchers found them with AI, through OpenAI's Patch the Planet program, per the BBC. Wiz called them the "most severe vulnerabilities ever discovered" by AI. Then the outages started: Finnish government services, the Dutch cyber agency's own site and some Wikimedia systems all went offline while teams patched.</p>
<h2>Where to follow it</h2>
<p>CISA's alert and PHP.net are the official sources. If you run a site, ask your host whether it's patched. On social, #PHP and #infosec are where developers are trading notes. Our <a href="/tech-ai/php2shell-vulnerability/">PHP2Shell guide</a> has the step-by-step checklist, and you can catch up on the <a href="/tech-ai/google-cloud-outage-revolut/">Google Cloud outage that took Revolut down</a>, <a href="/tech-ai/open-source-models/">open-weight AI models</a> and everything else in <a href="/tech-ai/">tech and AI</a>.</p>"""),
("world-series-game-1-2026-tonight","World Series Game 1 tonight: Rays vs. Brewers cheat sheet","World Series Game 1 is tonight at 8 p.m. ET on FOX. Starters, schedule, storylines and where to follow Rays vs. Brewers.","sports","world-series-2026","World Series: Rays vs. Brewers","WorldSeries",WS_SRC,
"""<p>Grab a seat: the World Series starts tonight, and whoever wins, a city celebrates its first-ever championship.</p>
<h2>What it is</h2>
<p>The <b>Tampa Bay Rays</b> visit the <b>Milwaukee Brewers</b> for Game 1 on <b>Friday, October 23, at 8 p.m. ET</b> at American Family Field, on FOX. MLB.com lists <b>Nick Martinez</b> for the Rays against <b>Jacob Misiorowski</b>, who threw 1,115 pitches of 100 mph or more this season.</p>
<table><tr><th>Game 1</th><td>Tonight, 8 p.m. ET, Milwaukee (FOX)</td></tr><tr><th>Game 2</th><td>Sat Oct 24, Milwaukee</td></tr><tr><th>Games 3 to 5</th><td>From Mon Oct 26, St. Petersburg</td></tr><tr><th>Games 6 and 7</th><td>Oct 30 and 31 in Milwaukee, if needed</td></tr></table>
<h2>Why it's trending</h2>
<p>It's the first World Series between two franchises that have never won it since 1980, per AP. Milwaukee won 103 games and hasn't been here since 1982, while Tampa Bay won 97 and is chasing the title it missed in 2008 and 2020. Christian Yelich summed up the mood to MLB.com: "our performance directly affects people's happiness and togetherness."</p>
<h2>Where to follow it</h2>
<p>Watch on FOX, FOX Deportes or FOX One, and follow #WorldSeries, #ThisIsMyCrew and #RaysUp. Our <a href="/sports/world-series-2026/">World Series 2026 guide</a> has the full schedule, and the <a href="/blog/rays-brewers-world-series-2026-preview/">series preview</a> covers both rosters. Busy sports weekend? The <a href="/sports/wnba-finals-2026/">WNBA Finals</a> resume Saturday with Atlanta up 2-1, and the <a href="/sports/nfl/">Bears just won on Thursday night</a>.</p>"""),
]
